// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_direct_8f.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: E-D — raster_program's tree-wide reg $0F scan (spec §4.2b).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "autoincrement"
//
// THE DODGE, spelled out. `RasterOp.SetReg($8F04)` is the enum variant reg_set
// returns, constructed by hand — so reg_set's ensure never runs and the stride
// change reaches the encoder with nothing having looked at it. The enum is `pub`
// (it has to be: the encoder's match arms are the public wire contract), so this is
// not a hypothetical spelling, it is one the language admits today.
//
// That is why the refusal is TWO layers. The constructor's ensure is the one that
// gives an author a good sentence at the call site; this scan is the one that cannot
// be dodged, and it runs on every program in the tree whether or not it has a band.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_four_bands.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_direct_8f

const POISON_DIRECT_8F = [
    fire(100, [RasterOp.SetReg($8F04)]),
]

ensure(raster_program(POISON_DIRECT_8F).len > 0,
       "poison_direct_8f: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
